course: dictionary
lesson: 15588
title: Synthesis: putting things together
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A synthesis is a mix of different things joined into one new whole. Think of a smoothie: you blend fruit, milk and yoghurt, and the result is one drink, not three separate pieces.
explain: The word has two parts. "Syn-" means together, and "thesis" means putting. So a synthesis is putting things together.
explain: The word has more than one meaning, so read the words around it. «The plant used photosynthesis to make its food.» Plants, light and food tell you this is about science.
fact: A synthesis is a mix or combination of different ideas, parts or things into one new whole.
fact: «Mia's project was a synthesis of ideas from three books.» She joined the ideas into one new summary.
fact: Photosynthesis is how plants make their own food from light, water and carbon dioxide.
fact: In science, synthesis can mean making a substance by joining simpler substances, in nature or in a lab.
fact: «Sound synthesis» means making sounds electronically, and a synthesiser is a machine that does this.
exercise: «Photosynthesis is how plants make food from light, water and carbon dioxide.» What is photosynthesis? | *How plants make their own food | A way of mixing paint colours | How rain falls from clouds | Making music with a computer
exercise: «Our history essay was a synthesis of letters, diaries and photos.» What does synthesis mean here? | A photo album of family holidays | *A new summary that brings ideas from several sources together | A list of only one source copied out
exercise: "Syn-" means together, and "thesis" means putting. What does synthesis mean? | Throwing things away | A pile of separate things left apart | *Putting things together into one whole | Breaking one thing into many pieces
test: «The chemist used synthesis to make a new medicine from simpler substances.» What does synthesis mean here? | Throwing old medicine away | *Making a substance by joining simpler substances | Breaking a medicine apart | Reading the label on a bottle
test: What does the "thesis" part of synthesis mean? | Breaking | Light | *Putting | Together
exam: Which sentence uses synthesis to mean making sounds electronically? | «The plant grew towards the sunny window.» | *«The musician played a synthesiser that made a low, buzzing sound.» | «The bread was baked for an hour.» | «The class wrote a synthesis of their favourite poems.»
